').write_text(f'''# Progress — {title}\\\\n\\\\n## Objective and constraints\\\\nBuild PLAN.md's original surgical action game; TASK.md governs deliverables. All development is in \"'`{base}/`; final single HTML and exit-interview.json go beside this log. Engine files remain read-only. No subagents.'\"\\\\n\\\\n## Decisions\\\\n- Title selected using Python secrets.randbelow from 50 candidates (index {i}).\\\\n- Full my-3dge workspace, deterministic seat-input simulation, eight story cases, extra session case, controller-first native mouse play.\\\\n- Native procedural 3D art and animations; all audio synthesized, music 10%.\\\\n\\\\n## Completed\\\\n- Read TASK.md and full PLAN.md.\\\\n- Confirmed upstream full-workspace bootstrap instructions.\\\\n\\\\n## Current / next\\\\n1. Bootstrap pinned engine and first one-file build + verification runner.\\\\n2. Deterministic surgery simulation, case data and winning bot.\\\\n3. 3D field, story cast, menus, sound, saves, co-op and hub.\\\\n4. Node/browser/hub playthroughs, cross-viewport checks, final feedback and packaging.\\\\n\\\\n## Environment\\\\n- Repo root: {Path.cwd()}\\\\n- Development folder: {base}\\\\n- The referenced ~/dev/TESTING-TOOLKIT.md does not exist; use supplied toolkit instructions and available Playwright.\\\\n- Use short private /tmp/g.* only for socket TMPDIR per PLAN §17.1; all artifacts under dev folder.\\\\n- Processes started: none.\\\\n''')\nprint(base)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Trauma-Coast-Second-Sight-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-040244\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
