{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'defineDevAction|interface DevAction|interface GeometrySpec|interface MaterialSpec|type ActionMapSpec' engine; rg --files engine | rg 'materials|pillar.ts|maps.ts'\"","aggregated_output":"engine/dev/actions.ts:7: *   engine's (engine/sim/devActions.ts: god, freeze, spawn, travel, timeScale, and any `defineDevAction` added), each\nengine/sim-api.ts:32:export { defineDevAction } from './sim/devActions';\nengine/gfx/geometry/geometry.ts:64:export interface GeometrySpec<S extends Schema = Schema> {\nengine/sim/devActions.ts:9: * anything changes. `__engine.actions` lists and runs them (engine/dev/actions.ts); `defineDevAction` adds a game's.\nengine/sim/devActions.ts:26: * `defineDevActionKinds(registry)` declares the kind, the component `invulnerable`, the setting `ai.frozen` and the\nengine/sim/devActions.ts:60:/** How a dev action is written: `defineDevAction(name, spec)`. */\nengine/sim/devActions.ts:61:export interface DevActionSpec {\nengine/sim/devActions.ts:226:export function defineDevActionKinds(registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): void {\nengine/sim/devActions.ts:232:    defineWith: \"defineDevAction('<name>', { help, args, run(w, args) })\",\nengine/sim/devActions.ts:240:  for (const [name, spec] of Object.entries(ENGINE_ACTIONS)) defineDevAction(name, spec, registry);\nengine/sim/devActions.ts:244:export function defineDevAction(name: string, spec: DevActionSpec, registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): DevAction {\nengine/sim/devActions.ts:245:  defineDevActionKinds(registry);\nengine/sim/devActions.ts:270:defineDevActionKinds();\nengine/sim/session.ts:47:    fix: \"add it to the scene, defineScene('{scene}', { actions: { {name}(w, args) { … } } }), or to the engine's, defineDevAction('{name}', { help, run }) (engine/sim/devActions.ts); or call one there is\",\nengine/gfx/geometry/pillar.ts\nengine/gfx/materials/nodeCopy.ts\nengine/gfx/materials/compile.ts\nengine/gfx/materials/styles.ts\nengine/gfx/materials/builtins.ts\nengine/gfx/materials/outline.ts\nengine/gfx/materials/material.ts\nengine/gfx/materials/library.ts\nengine/gfx/materials/toon.ts\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nPath('labs/game/view/assets.ts').write_text('''/** @file Original Harbor Light materials, looks and procedural hospital props on the engine geometry kit. */\nimport {defineMaterial,defineLook,defineSky,defineTexture,defineGeometry,roundedBoxGeometry} from '../../../engine';\nexport const PALETTE={teal:'#164b4d',navy:'#071a22',brass:'#bd965c',steel:'#b7cdd3',cream:'#e8e4cf',red:'#7e2637',glow:'#75f3cf'};\nfor(const [name,color] of Object.entries(PALETTE))defineMaterial(\"'`material:hl-${name}`,{color,roughness:name==='\"'steel'?.2:.6,metalness:name==='steel'?.7:name==='brass'?.45:0});\ndefineMaterial('material:hl-lit',{color:'#8de8cf',emissive:'#7bdcbd',emissiveIntensity:1.4,roughness:.3});\ndefineMaterial('material:hl-window',{color:'#153544',emissive:'#0a2638',emissiveIntensity:.3,roughness:.2});\ndefineMaterial('material:tissue',{color:'#ffffff',vertexColors:true,roughness:.34,metalness:.03});\ndefineMaterial('material:wet',{color:'#ffffff',vertexColors:true,roughness:.19,metalness:.12});\ndefineMaterial('material:thread',{color:'#ffffff',vertexColors:true,roughness:.45});\ndefineMaterial('material:field-glow',{color:'#ffffff',vertexColors:true,emissive:'#6bd8cc',emissiveIntensity:.45,roughness:.25});\ndefineMaterial('material:field-steel',{color:'#ffffff',vertexColors:true,roughness:.2,metalness:.8});\ndefineMaterial('material:field-glove',{color:'#ffffff',vertexColors:true,roughness:.7});\ndefineTexture('texture:wet-cells',{description:'Fine cells and microheight in living tissue.',width:128,height:128,seed:4,texel:({x,y})=>{const v=.8+.1*Math.sin(x*.61)*Math.sin(y*.57);return {color:[v,v*.92,v*.9],height:v*.04};}});\ndefineGeometry('geometry:hl-rounded',{description:'Soft machined hospital furniture.',create:()=>roundedBoxGeometry({width:1,height:1,depth:1,radius:.1})});\ndefineSky('sky:harbor',{background:'#07151c',pointLights:1,ambient:{sky:'#bcdfdf',ground:'#476067',intensity:1.4},sun:{color:'#ffe4c4',intensity:2.8,azimuth:3.7,elevation:1.1},fog:{color:'#091e28',amount:.3,start:22,end:65}});\ndefineLook('look:field',{description:'Glossy living tissue under a surgical lamp.',style:'pbr',sky:'sky:harbor',resolution:'full',textures:'smooth',filters:{ao:{scope:'all',strength:.6},aa:{scope:'all'},bloom:{scope:'all',strength:.15}}});\ndefineLook('look:harbor',{description:'Sea-glass walls, brass lamps and storm blue.',style:'toon',sky:'sky:harbor',resolution:'full',textures:'smooth',filters:{ao:{scope:'all',strength:.4},aa:{scope:'all'},bloom:{scope:'all',strength:.18}}});\ndefineLook('look:stillpoint',{description:'A silent teal moment between heartbeats.',filters:{vignette:{scope:'all',strength:.4},grade:{scope:'all',saturation:.3}}});\ndefineLook('look:second-pulse',{description:'Amber heat and the rush of certainty.',filters:{speedlines:{scope:'all',strength:.3}}});\n''')\nPath('labs/game/cast/props.ts').write_text('''/** @file Hospital sets and surgical framing, as ordinary engine props; no engine assets are modified. */\nimport {defineProp,spawnProp,type PropPart,type World} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nconst box=(name:string,size:[number,number,number],at:[number,number,number],mat='teal',rotation:[number,number,number]=[0,0,0]):Partial<PropPart>=>({name,geometry:'geometry:box',params:{width:size[0],height:size[1],depth:size[2]},material:\"'`material:hl-${mat}`,position:at,rotation});\nconst tube=(name:string,radius:number,height:number,at:[number,number,number],mat='\"'steel'):Partial<PropPart>=>({name,geometry:'geometry:pillar',params:{radius,height,sides:16},material:\"'`material:hl-${mat}`,position:at});\nconst room:Partial<PropPart>[]=[box('\"'floor',[24,.18,22],[-12,-.22,-10],'navy'),box('back-wall',[24,6,.3],[-12,0,7],'teal'),box('left-wall',[.3,6,18],[-10,0,-10],'teal'),box('window',[7,3.7,.12],[.7,1.5,6.8],'window'),box('window-frame',[7.4,.09,.18],[.5,3.3,6.6],'brass')];\nfor(let i=0;i<12;i++)room.push(box(\"'`tile-${i}`,[.018,.01,19],[-10+i*2,-.02,-10],'\"'steel'));\nfor(let i=0;i<4;i++)room.push(box(\"'`window-bar-${i}`,[.06,3.9,.18],[1.3+i*1.9,1.4,6.6],'\"'brass'));\ndefineProp('prop:harbor-room',{description:'The rain-lit Harbor Light operating room.',parts:room});\ndefineProp('prop:operating-table',{description:'Padded operating table and steel pedestal.',parts:[box('pedestal',[1.1,1.15,1.5],[-.55,0,-.75],'steel'),box('bed',[3.1,.2,6],[-1.55,1.15,-3],'steel'),box('mattress',[2.9,.2,5.9],[-1.45,1.35,-2.95],'navy'),box('drape',[2.85,.08,4.1],[-1.42,1.58,-1.45],'teal'),box('pillow',[2,.14,1.2],[-1,1.55,-2.8],'cream')]});\ndefineProp('prop:surgical-lamp',{description:'Six petal surgical lamp, a sculptural halo of warm light.',parts:[tube('stand',.06,4.5,[0,0,0]),box('arm',[3.2,.08,.08],[0,4.4,0],'steel'),...Array.from({length:6},(_,i)=>tube(\"'`petal-${i}`,.38,.12,[3+Math.cos(i*Math.PI/3)*.65,4.35,Math.sin(i*Math.PI/3)*.65],'\"'lit'))],light:{tag:'surgical',color:'#fff0da',intensity:45,distance:20,position:[3,3.5,0]}});\ndefineProp('prop:heart-monitor',{description:'Brass-framed bedside heart monitor.',parts:[tube('stem',.05,1.4,[0,0,0]),box('monitor',[1.5,1.05,.25],[-.75,1.4,0],'navy'),box('display',[1.3,.8,.03],[-.65,1.53,-.04],'window'),box('trace',[1.16,.025,.015],[-.58,1.92,-.06],'lit'),tube('foot',.45,.06,[0,0,0])],light:{tag:'monitor',color:'#6affd4',intensity:4,distance:5,position:[0,1.9,0]}});\ndefineProp('prop:iv',{description:'IV stand with suspended stabilizer.',parts:[tube('pole',.035,2.6,[0,0,0]),box('hook',[.8,.04,.04],[-.4,2.55,0],'steel'),box('bag',[.4,.6,.13],[-.34,1.85,0],'cream'),tube('base',.4,.04,[0,0,0])]});\ndefineProp('prop:tray',{description:'Sterile instrument trolley.',parts:[box('top',[2.2,.08,1.1],[-1.1,1.05,-.55],'steel'),box('liner',[2,.03,.9],[-1,1.14,-.45],'teal'),...[-.9,.9].map((x,i)=>tube(\"'`leg-${i}`,.035,1.08,[x,0,0])),...Array.from({length:6},(_,i)=>box(`instrument-${i}`,[.06,.03,.65],[-.7+i*.26,1.19,-.32],'\"'steel'))]});\ndefineProp('prop:desk',{description:'The Chief’s heavy desk or the gala lectern.',parts:[box('desk',[4,.2,1.6],[-2,1.2,-.8],'brass'),box('leg-l',[.18,1.2,1.3],[-1.8,0,-.65],'navy'),box('leg-r',[.18,1.2,1.3],[1.6,0,-.65],'navy'),box('files',[.8,.08,.6],[.5,1.43,-.3],'cream')]});\ndefineProp('prop:television',{description:'Halcyon ward screen.',parts:[box('tv',[3.8,2.1,.25],[-1.9,2,0],'navy'),box('screen',[3.5,1.8,.03],[-1.75,2.15,-.04],'window'),box('halcyon',[1.8,.06,.02],[-.9,3.1,-.08],'lit')]});\nconst frame:Partial<PropPart>[]=[box('table',[21,.3,13],[-10.5,-.5,-6.5],'steel')];\nfor(const x of [-7.4,7.4])for(const z of [-2,2]){frame.push(box(\"'`clamp-${x}-${z}`,[.3,.12,.8],[x,.18,z],'\"'steel',[0,0,x<0?-.15:.15]));frame.push(tube(\"'`screw-${x}-${z}`,.15,.1,[x,.35,z+.2],'\"'brass'));}\ndefineProp('prop:field-frame',{description:'The sterile drape’s machined clamps.',parts:frame,light:{tag:'surgical',color:'#ffedd2',intensity:60,distance:28,position:[0,8,-1]}});\nexport function stage<C extends object>(w:World<C>,set:string):void{\n if(set==='field'){for(const id of ['sheet','wet','thread','glow','steel','glove'])spawnProp(w,{prop:\"'`prop:live-${id}`,at:[0,0,0]});spawnProp(w,{prop:'\"'prop:field-frame',at:[0,0,0]});return;}\n spawnProp(w,{prop:'prop:harbor-room',at:[0,0,0]});\n spawnProp(w,{prop:'prop:operating-table',at:[0,0,1],yaw:.25});spawnProp(w,{prop:'prop:surgical-lamp',at:[-4,0,1]});\n for(const [prop,x,z] of [['heart-monitor',3,1],['iv',-2.7,2],['tray',3,-2]] as [string,number,number][])spawnProp(w,{prop:\"'`prop:${prop}`,at:[x,0,z]});\n spawnProp(w,{prop:'\"'prop:television',at:[4,0,6.3]});\n if(['chief','gala','ship'].includes(set))spawnProp(w,{prop:'prop:desk',at:[-3,0,2]});\n}\n''')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nPath('labs/game/view/assets.ts').write_text('''/** @file Original Harbor Light materials, looks and procedural hospital props on the engine geometry kit. */\nimport {defineMaterial,defineLook,defineSky,defineTexture,defineGeometry,roundedBoxGeometry} from '../../../engine';\nexport const PALETTE={teal:'#164b4d',navy:'#071a22',brass:'#bd965c',steel:'#b7cdd3',cream:'#e8e4cf',red:'#7e2637',glow:'#75f3cf'};\nfor(const [name,color] of Object.entries(PALETTE))defineMaterial(\"'`material:hl-${name}`,{color,roughness:name==='\"'steel'?.2:.6,metalness:name==='steel'?.7:name==='brass'?.45:0});\ndefineMaterial('material:hl-lit',{color:'#8de8cf',emissive:'#7bdcbd',emissiveIntensity:1.4,roughness:.3});\ndefineMaterial('material:hl-window',{color:'#153544',emissive:'#0a2638',emissiveIntensity:.3,roughness:.2});\ndefineMaterial('material:tissue',{color:'#ffffff',vertexColors:true,roughness:.34,metalness:.03});\ndefineMaterial('material:wet',{color:'#ffffff',vertexColors:true,roughness:.19,metalness:.12});\ndefineMaterial('material:thread',{color:'#ffffff',vertexColors:true,roughness:.45});\ndefineMaterial('material:field-glow',{color:'#ffffff',vertexColors:true,emissive:'#6bd8cc',emissiveIntensity:.45,roughness:.25});\ndefineMaterial('material:field-steel',{color:'#ffffff',vertexColors:true,roughness:.2,metalness:.8});\ndefineMaterial('material:field-glove',{color:'#ffffff',vertexColors:true,roughness:.7});\ndefineTexture('texture:wet-cells',{description:'Fine cells and microheight in living tissue.',width:128,height:128,seed:4,texel:({x,y})=>{const v=.8+.1*Math.sin(x*.61)*Math.sin(y*.57);return {color:[v,v*.92,v*.9],height:v*.04};}});\ndefineGeometry('geometry:hl-rounded',{description:'Soft machined hospital furniture.',create:()=>roundedBoxGeometry({width:1,height:1,depth:1,radius:.1})});\ndefineSky('sky:harbor',{background:'#07151c',pointLights:1,ambient:{sky:'#bcdfdf',ground:'#476067',intensity:1.4},sun:{color:'#ffe4c4',intensity:2.8,azimuth:3.7,elevation:1.1},fog:{color:'#091e28',amount:.3,start:22,end:65}});\ndefineLook('look:field',{description:'Glossy living tissue under a surgical lamp.',style:'pbr',sky:'sky:harbor',resolution:'full',textures:'smooth',filters:{ao:{scope:'all',strength:.6},aa:{scope:'all'},bloom:{scope:'all',strength:.15}}});\ndefineLook('look:harbor',{description:'Sea-glass walls, brass lamps and storm blue.',style:'toon',sky:'sky:harbor',resolution:'full',textures:'smooth',filters:{ao:{scope:'all',strength:.4},aa:{scope:'all'},bloom:{scope:'all',strength:.18}}});\ndefineLook('look:stillpoint',{description:'A silent teal moment between heartbeats.',filters:{vignette:{scope:'all',strength:.4},grade:{scope:'all',saturation:.3}}});\ndefineLook('look:second-pulse',{description:'Amber heat and the rush of certainty.',filters:{speedlines:{scope:'all',strength:.3}}});\n''')\nPath('labs/game/cast/props.ts').write_text('''/** @file Hospital sets and surgical framing, as ordinary engine props; no engine assets are modified. */\nimport {defineProp,spawnProp,type PropPart,type World} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nconst box=(name:string,size:[number,number,number],at:[number,number,number],mat='teal',rotation:[number,number,number]=[0,0,0]):Partial<PropPart>=>({name,geometry:'geometry:box',params:{width:size[0],height:size[1],depth:size[2]},material:\"'`material:hl-${mat}`,position:at,rotation});\nconst tube=(name:string,radius:number,height:number,at:[number,number,number],mat='\"'steel'):Partial<PropPart>=>({name,geometry:'geometry:pillar',params:{radius,height,sides:16},material:\"'`material:hl-${mat}`,position:at});\nconst room:Partial<PropPart>[]=[box('\"'floor',[24,.18,22],[-12,-.22,-10],'navy'),box('back-wall',[24,6,.3],[-12,0,7],'teal'),box('left-wall',[.3,6,18],[-10,0,-10],'teal'),box('window',[7,3.7,.12],[.7,1.5,6.8],'window'),box('window-frame',[7.4,.09,.18],[.5,3.3,6.6],'brass')];\nfor(let i=0;i<12;i++)room.push(box(\"'`tile-${i}`,[.018,.01,19],[-10+i*2,-.02,-10],'\"'steel'));\nfor(let i=0;i<4;i++)room.push(box(\"'`window-bar-${i}`,[.06,3.9,.18],[1.3+i*1.9,1.4,6.6],'\"'brass'));\ndefineProp('prop:harbor-room',{description:'The rain-lit Harbor Light operating room.',parts:room});\ndefineProp('prop:operating-table',{description:'Padded operating table and steel pedestal.',parts:[box('pedestal',[1.1,1.15,1.5],[-.55,0,-.75],'steel'),box('bed',[3.1,.2,6],[-1.55,1.15,-3],'steel'),box('mattress',[2.9,.2,5.9],[-1.45,1.35,-2.95],'navy'),box('drape',[2.85,.08,4.1],[-1.42,1.58,-1.45],'teal'),box('pillow',[2,.14,1.2],[-1,1.55,-2.8],'cream')]});\ndefineProp('prop:surgical-lamp',{description:'Six petal surgical lamp, a sculptural halo of warm light.',parts:[tube('stand',.06,4.5,[0,0,0]),box('arm',[3.2,.08,.08],[0,4.4,0],'steel'),...Array.from({length:6},(_,i)=>tube(\"'`petal-${i}`,.38,.12,[3+Math.cos(i*Math.PI/3)*.65,4.35,Math.sin(i*Math.PI/3)*.65],'\"'lit'))],light:{tag:'surgical',color:'#fff0da',intensity:45,distance:20,position:[3,3.5,0]}});\ndefineProp('prop:heart-monitor',{description:'Brass-framed bedside heart monitor.',parts:[tube('stem',.05,1.4,[0,0,0]),box('monitor',[1.5,1.05,.25],[-.75,1.4,0],'navy'),box('display',[1.3,.8,.03],[-.65,1.53,-.04],'window'),box('trace',[1.16,.025,.015],[-.58,1.92,-.06],'lit'),tube('foot',.45,.06,[0,0,0])],light:{tag:'monitor',color:'#6affd4',intensity:4,distance:5,position:[0,1.9,0]}});\ndefineProp('prop:iv',{description:'IV stand with suspended stabilizer.',parts:[tube('pole',.035,2.6,[0,0,0]),box('hook',[.8,.04,.04],[-.4,2.55,0],'steel'),box('bag',[.4,.6,.13],[-.34,1.85,0],'cream'),tube('base',.4,.04,[0,0,0])]});\ndefineProp('prop:tray',{description:'Sterile instrument trolley.',parts:[box('top',[2.2,.08,1.1],[-1.1,1.05,-.55],'steel'),box('liner',[2,.03,.9],[-1,1.14,-.45],'teal'),...[-.9,.9].map((x,i)=>tube(\"'`leg-${i}`,.035,1.08,[x,0,0])),...Array.from({length:6},(_,i)=>box(`instrument-${i}`,[.06,.03,.65],[-.7+i*.26,1.19,-.32],'\"'steel'))]});\ndefineProp('prop:desk',{description:'The Chief’s heavy desk or the gala lectern.',parts:[box('desk',[4,.2,1.6],[-2,1.2,-.8],'brass'),box('leg-l',[.18,1.2,1.3],[-1.8,0,-.65],'navy'),box('leg-r',[.18,1.2,1.3],[1.6,0,-.65],'navy'),box('files',[.8,.08,.6],[.5,1.43,-.3],'cream')]});\ndefineProp('prop:television',{description:'Halcyon ward screen.',parts:[box('tv',[3.8,2.1,.25],[-1.9,2,0],'navy'),box('screen',[3.5,1.8,.03],[-1.75,2.15,-.04],'window'),box('halcyon',[1.8,.06,.02],[-.9,3.1,-.08],'lit')]});\nconst frame:Partial<PropPart>[]=[box('table',[21,.3,13],[-10.5,-.5,-6.5],'steel')];\nfor(const x of [-7.4,7.4])for(const z of [-2,2]){frame.push(box(\"'`clamp-${x}-${z}`,[.3,.12,.8],[x,.18,z],'\"'steel',[0,0,x<0?-.15:.15]));frame.push(tube(\"'`screw-${x}-${z}`,.15,.1,[x,.35,z+.2],'\"'brass'));}\ndefineProp('prop:field-frame',{description:'The sterile drape’s machined clamps.',parts:frame,light:{tag:'surgical',color:'#ffedd2',intensity:60,distance:28,position:[0,8,-1]}});\nexport function stage<C extends object>(w:World<C>,set:string):void{\n if(set==='field'){for(const id of ['sheet','wet','thread','glow','steel','glove'])spawnProp(w,{prop:\"'`prop:live-${id}`,at:[0,0,0]});spawnProp(w,{prop:'\"'prop:field-frame',at:[0,0,0]});return;}\n spawnProp(w,{prop:'prop:harbor-room',at:[0,0,0]});\n spawnProp(w,{prop:'prop:operating-table',at:[0,0,1],yaw:.25});spawnProp(w,{prop:'prop:surgical-lamp',at:[-4,0,1]});\n for(const [prop,x,z] of [['heart-monitor',3,1],['iv',-2.7,2],['tray',3,-2]] as [string,number,number][])spawnProp(w,{prop:\"'`prop:${prop}`,at:[x,0,z]});\n spawnProp(w,{prop:'\"'prop:television',at:[4,0,6.3]});\n if(['chief','gala','ship'].includes(set))spawnProp(w,{prop:'prop:desk',at:[-3,0,2]});\n}\n''')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '55,110p' engine/gfx/textures/types.ts; sed -n '60,95p' engine/gfx/geometry/geometry.ts; sed -n '20,65p' engine/gfx/geometry/pillar.ts; sed -n '58,90p' engine/sim/devActions.ts; sed -n '170,190p' docs/GAME-GUIDE.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '55,110p' engine/gfx/textures/types.ts; sed -n '60,95p' engine/gfx/geometry/geometry.ts; sed -n '20,65p' engine/gfx/geometry/pillar.ts; sed -n '58,90p' engine/sim/devActions.ts; sed -n '170,190p' docs/GAME-GUIDE.md\"","aggregated_output":"/** How a texture is magnified: `pixel` keeps texels crisp (nearest), `smooth` blends them (linear). */\nexport type TextureLook = (typeof TEXTURE_LOOKS)[number];\n\n/** A generator: its parameters, the size and look it bakes at, and the function that writes its texels. */\nexport interface TextureSpec<S extends Schema = Schema> {\n  /** What it draws, in plain sentences. */\n  description: string;\n  /** Its parameters, as schema fields (engine/core/schema.ts), each with its default. */\n  params?: S;\n  /** The size it bakes at by default, [width, height] in texels: one period of the pattern. */\n  size?: [number, number];\n  /** The smallest size the pattern repeats at, given the parameters; a bake size must be a multiple of it. */\n  tile?: (params: EntryOf<S>) => [number, number];\n  /** Texels per metre, on geometry whose UVs are in metres (WP 2.4's builders); 16 by default. */\n  density?: number;\n  /** How it is magnified; `pixel` by default. */\n  look?: TextureLook;\n  /** The generator: called once per bake, it returns the function that writes each texel. */\n  create: (context: TextureContext<EntryOf<S>>) => TexelFn;\n}\n\n/** Returns `spec` unchanged, typed: `create` sees the parameters as the schema `params` declares them. */\nexport function textureSpec<const S extends Schema>(spec: TextureSpec<S>): TextureSpec<S> {\n  return spec;\n}\n  params?: Record<string, unknown>;\n}\n\n/** What `defineGeometry` takes: the entry's fields (`params` and `budget` have defaults), `create` typed by `params`. */\nexport interface GeometrySpec<S extends Schema = Schema> {\n  /** What it is, in plain sentences. */\n  description: string;\n  /** Its parameters, as schema fields (engine/core/schema.ts), each with its default. */\n  params?: S;\n  /** The most vertices it may have at its defaults; 4096 by default. */\n  budget?: number;\n  /** The builder: every parameter filled, as `params` declares them. */\n  create: (params: EntryOf<S>) => BufferGeometry;\n}\n\n/** The problems of a geometry beyond its fields: its parameter schema. */\nfunction geometryProblems(entry: GeometryEntry): string[] {\n  if (!isPlainObject(entry.params)) return ['params must be an object of schema fields'];\n  const problems: string[] = [];\n  for (const [key, field] of Object.entries(entry.params)) {\n    problems.push(...checkField(field, `params.${key}`).map((problem) => problem.message));\n    if (isPlainObject(field) && field.default === undefined) {\n      problems.push(`params.${key} needs a default: a prop may leave any parameter out`);\n    }\n  }\n  return problems;\n}\n\n/** Declares the kind `geometry` on `registry`, with the kit's built-in shapes, unless it has it. */\nexport function geometryKind(registry: Registry): void {\n  if (registry.kinds().includes('geometry')) return;\n  registry.defineKind('geometry', {\n    description:\n      'Shapes props, levels and bodies name by id: a builder of a three.js BufferGeometry with its parameters and a vertex budget.',\n    fields: GEOMETRY_FIELDS,\n    fallback: 'geometry:box',\nimport type { BufferGeometry } from 'three/webgpu';\nimport { boxGeometry } from './box';\nimport { assertSizes } from './checks';\nimport { mergeGeometries, sidesThenTops } from './groups';\n\n/** A pillar's footprint and height in metres. */\nexport interface PillarOptions {\n  /** The footprint's side: two tiles of 1 m. */\n  width?: number;\n  height?: number;\n}\n\n/** One part of a pillar: a square slab `width` across, from height `from` to `to` (m). */\nexport interface PillarPart {\n  name: 'plinth' | 'shaft' | 'capital' | 'abacus';\n  width: number;\n  from: number;\n  to: number;\n}\n\n/** The prototype's parts in its units: [name, width of 32, from, to of 56]. */\nconst PARTS: readonly [PillarPart['name'], number, number, number][] = [\n  ['plinth', 34, 0, 6],\n  ['shaft', 28, 6, 48],\n  ['capital', 34, 48, 52],\n  ['abacus', 38, 52, 56],\n];\n\n/** A pillar's parts, bottom to top (see the file comment). Throws `GFX_BAD_GEOMETRY` for a size ≤ 0. */\nexport function pillarParts({ width = 2, height = 3.5 }: PillarOptions = {}): PillarPart[] {\n  assertSizes('pillar', { width, height });\n  return PARTS.map(([name, across, from, to]) => ({\n    name,\n    width: (width * across) / 32,\n    from: (height * from) / 56,\n    to: (height * to) / 56,\n  }));\n}\n\n/** A pillar as one geometry standing on the ground: its parts' boxes, sides then tops. */\nexport function pillarGeometry(options: PillarOptions = {}): BufferGeometry {\n  const boxes = pillarParts(options).map(({ width, from, to }) => {\n    const box = boxGeometry({ width, height: to - from, depth: width });\n    return box.translate(0, from, 0);\n  });\n  const merged = sidesThenTops(mergeGeometries(boxes));\n});\n\n/** How a dev action is written: `defineDevAction(name, spec)`. */\nexport interface DevActionSpec {\n  /** What it does, one line: `__engine.actions.list()` shows it. */\n  help: string;\n  /** Its arguments, name → schema field: checked, defaults filled, before it runs. */\n  args?: Schema;\n  /** What it changes in the sim, inside `w.run`, between steps: recorded as a dev action. */\n  run?: (w: World, args: Record<string, unknown>) => void;\n  /** The settings it sets, by path: through the session, recorded unless view. */\n  settings?: (args: Record<string, unknown>) => Record<string, SettingValue>;\n}\n\n/** A registered dev action: its spec, plus `id` (its name) and `kind`. */\nexport type DevAction = Entry & Required<DevActionSpec>;\n\n/** What an entry without a `run` changes in the sim: nothing, and it is not recorded as a dev action. */\nconst NO_RUN = (): void => {};\n/** What an entry without `settings` sets: nothing. */\nconst NO_SETTINGS = (): Record<string, SettingValue> => ({});\n\n/** The fields of a `devAction` entry. */\nconst DEV_ACTION_FIELDS = {\n  help: { type: 'string', required: true, description: 'What it does, one line: __engine.actions.list() shows it.' },\n  args: {\n    type: 'object',\n    default: {},\n    description:\n      'Its arguments, name → schema field (engine/core/schema.ts): checked, defaults filled, before it runs.',\n  },\n  run: {\n    type: 'function',\n\n## 7. Testing a game\n\n- The starter's test shows the four kinds every game keeps: its golden replay, a run that continues exactly after a\n  capture and a restore, the bot winning on 10 seeds, and a rule (the clock). Tests sit beside their module\n  (`play.test.ts`) and run with `npm test`.\n- Keep the bot as the game grows: teach it each new rule. \"The bot wins on 10 seeds\" keeps proving the game can be won,\n  and finds the seeds that softlock.\n- Check the UI through the DOM: the overlay's elements are `[data-ui]` (`node x inspect`, then `node x eval`).\n- When play changes on purpose, record the goldens again (`node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim --update`) and\n  say why in the commit. When a hash changes by surprise, `node x replay <file> --browser sim --bisect` narrows it\n  down: to the step, entity and field where two runs part (Node and Chromium, or Node and Node again), or, when every\n  run agrees but they all left the goldens, to the checkpoints between which they did (then the code, data or a\n  dependency changed what the sim does). The usual causes: a `Math` function held in a variable, `**`, an iteration\n  whose order is not fixed, module state between runs, view settings or presentation reaching the sim, `async` code in\n  a step.\n\n## 8. Looking things up\n\n- **docs/API.md**: every public name with the first sentence of its doc comment, the public API first. The comment at\n  the link is the full manual: grep engine/ for the name.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
