{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_74","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\ninfo={\n'sourceInformation':{'date':'2026-11-05 04:02:44','source':'Trauma Center: Second Opinion','plan':'PLAN.md','genre':'Simulation / surgical action','perspective':'First-person operating field; staged third-person story scenes','tech':'my-3dge 6a1501f, three.js 0.182.0 WebGPU, Rapier 0.21.0, TypeScript 5.9.3, Vite 7.3.7, AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.4.0','artDirection':'Original procedural Harbor Light hospital: sea-glass teal, brass and rain blue; glossy stylized tissue; native engine geometry and puppets','animation':'Native humanoid and multi-beat action animator, blob rigs, live tissue and instrument geometry','audio':'Original synthesized adaptive music, instrument effects, ECG and offline-rendered formant gibberish voices; music defaults to 10%','online':'AI Hub shared-world sessions only; 1–4 local surgeons in couch co-op on one screen','testing':'Headless deterministic simulation, bot playthroughs, replay hashes, browser interaction and AI Hub harness; no review agents. Physical controllers, audio listening, TV and real iOS Safari unavailable.','research':'Supplied PLAN.md research; upstream my-3dge workspace and public API; AI Hub Session Protocol v1 documentation.','environment':'Codex CLI (headless); Linux','model':'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort max','usage':'added on import'},\n 'testingFeedback':['unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown'],\n 'engineFeedback':['The deterministic headless core and readable procedural geometry make surgical rules and presentation separable.','The public API uses explicit prop yaw and constrained geometry parameters; type checks caught mistaken signatures.','A gesture-based surgical simulation, live tissue meshes, multi-site triage, parasite state machines and host-sequenced co-op.','Animating live geometry requires retaining builder buffers; multi-device seats and surgical aiming need game-owned input.','None. Engine files remain read-only; local engine patches are empty.','Add a supported dynamic geometry handle with buffer updates and explicit bounds.'],\n 'promptFeedback':['A concrete surgical world, controls, cases and testable completion criteria.','The referenced machine-wide testing toolkit document is absent; supplied instructions provided the needed alternatives.','Making every surgical tool, strain, story case, controller input and multiplayer session share one reproducible simulation.','Separate essential slice requirements from suggested tuning and give one canonical acceptance checklist.'],\n 'aiHub':{'name':'Trauma Coast: Second Sight','tagline':'The night shift has a pulse.','description':'Eight operations in a storm-struck harbor hospital. Cut, stitch and fight the soothingly named parasites in miracle grafts, alone or with up to four surgeons.','type':'Game','genre':'Simulation','source':'Trauma Center: Second Opinion','series':'Trauma Center','players':'1–4','controls':'Stick or mouse aims · R2 or click uses the tool · right stick or 1–8 picks a tool','tags':['3d','first-person','co-op','story','boss fights','comedy']}}\nPath('../exit-interview.json').write_text(json.dumps(info,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPath('labs/game/data/about.ts').write_text('/** @file Catalogue and feedback data shared verbatim with the exit interview. */\\\\nexport const interview = '+json.dumps(info,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+' as const;\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_74","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\ninfo={\n'sourceInformation':{'date':'2026-11-05 04:02:44','source':'Trauma Center: Second Opinion','plan':'PLAN.md','genre':'Simulation / surgical action','perspective':'First-person operating field; staged third-person story scenes','tech':'my-3dge 6a1501f, three.js 0.182.0 WebGPU, Rapier 0.21.0, TypeScript 5.9.3, Vite 7.3.7, AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.4.0','artDirection':'Original procedural Harbor Light hospital: sea-glass teal, brass and rain blue; glossy stylized tissue; native engine geometry and puppets','animation':'Native humanoid and multi-beat action animator, blob rigs, live tissue and instrument geometry','audio':'Original synthesized adaptive music, instrument effects, ECG and offline-rendered formant gibberish voices; music defaults to 10%','online':'AI Hub shared-world sessions only; 1–4 local surgeons in couch co-op on one screen','testing':'Headless deterministic simulation, bot playthroughs, replay hashes, browser interaction and AI Hub harness; no review agents. Physical controllers, audio listening, TV and real iOS Safari unavailable.','research':'Supplied PLAN.md research; upstream my-3dge workspace and public API; AI Hub Session Protocol v1 documentation.','environment':'Codex CLI (headless); Linux','model':'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort max','usage':'added on import'},\n 'testingFeedback':['unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown'],\n 'engineFeedback':['The deterministic headless core and readable procedural geometry make surgical rules and presentation separable.','The public API uses explicit prop yaw and constrained geometry parameters; type checks caught mistaken signatures.','A gesture-based surgical simulation, live tissue meshes, multi-site triage, parasite state machines and host-sequenced co-op.','Animating live geometry requires retaining builder buffers; multi-